        "original_id": "2d219b65-fd12-5bd0-a629-df91f49b2928",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Frailea, Cyathodes, Frailea castanea, Gymnocalycium eurypleurum\n- Plant groups: cacti, shrubs, heath family\n- Places: Brazil, Argentina, Uruguay\n\nFacts:\n- Frailea is a genus of globular to short cylindrical cacti native to Brazil.\n- Cyathodes is a genus of shrubs in the heath family.\n- Frailea castanea is a species of Frailea found in Argentina, Brazil, and Uruguay.\n- Gymnocalycium eurypleurum is almost always solitary in the wild and may grow in association with Frailea species.",
